    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175-a1">

                <pb facs="0352" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg252"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Teller to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of the Interior</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 14, 1884.</date>
                        (Received July 15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence upon
                    the subject, and more particularly to your letter of the 16th ultimo, I have the
                    honor to inclose herewith a copy of a letter from the governor of Washington
                    Territory in the matter of the alleged lynching of the Indian boy “Jack,” in
                    British Columbia, by American citizens from Washington Territory.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>H. M. TELLER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
